// [nonmatching] Phase 11: tetrahedral type-0/type-1 stage diagnostic.
//
// The matching tet/tet M0 comparison (tests/nonmatching/phase11_matching_compare.m)
// differed by 7.70e-9 (p = 1) and 2.06e-8 (p = 2), whereas hexahedra agree to
// about 1e-15. The conformal (type 0) path and the base HDG face integrals use
// the master-element face tables written to master.bin (shapfgt, shapfgw,
// shapfnt, shapfn), generated by mkshape/koornwinder. The type-1 setup
// evaluates donor face values with its own SurfaceNodalBasis. This test
// compares the data both paths consume, stage by stage, against an
// independent long-double Lagrange reference built on the exact lattice
// coordinates of the master nodes:
//
//   1. topology/ordering  face-node permutation and face-plane membership
//   2. geometry           stored master node coordinates vs the exact lattice
//   3. basis              face tables at the face Gauss points (master table
//                         vs type-1 SurfaceNodalBasis vs reference); volume
//                         table at the Gauss points; derivative table at the
//                         nodes (reported only, not used by the solve)
//   4. trace interp.      a degree-p trace interpolated to the Gauss points
//   5. face integration   int psi_i g dS, the quantity the conformal exchange
//                         and the type-1 owner assembly both build
//
// Differences are reported as absolute, relative and scaled ULP
// (|a - b| / (eps max(|a|, |b|, 1))). The first stage whose master-table data
// differ from the reference by more than the M0 criterion 5e-12 is printed as
// the first diverging stage.
//
// Assertions: the type-1 surface basis must reproduce the reference to 1e-12
// for every family and order, the hexahedral master tables to 1e-12, and the
// tetrahedral master tables to the M0 criterion 5e-12. The tetrahedral check
// guards the collapsed-vertex fix in koornwinder2d (Phase 11 master-basis
// amendment); --report-only disables it for diagnosis.

